<back><div type="verses">
<lg label="2."><l>I hardly know myself;</l><l>Deceived so much by pride,</l><l>I often think I’m right</l><l>And am self-satisfied.</l></lg>
<lg label="3."><l>I know Thee even less;</l><l>In doctrine, shallowly;</l><l>True revelation lack</l><l>Of Thy reality.</l></lg>
<lg label="4."><l>As for Thy life within,</l><l>In darkness I mistake—</l><l>If spirit or the flesh,</l><l>One for the other take.</l></lg>
<lg label="5."><l>As for Thy way, O Lord,</l><l>I often am not clear;</l><l>I toward seclusion tend</l><l>And from the pathway veer.</l></lg>
<lg label="6."><l>As for Thy will for me,</l><l>I do not know it well;</l><l>I substitute my own</l><l>And often would rebel.</l></lg>
<lg label="7."><l>As for the church, I need</l><l>Thy revelation more,</l><l>The Body-life to know,</l><l>Thy wisdom to explore.</l></lg>
<lg label="8."><l>I long to be unveiled,</l><l>In everything made clear,</l><l>No more to be deceived</l><l>Or to my pride adhere.</l></lg>
</div>
</back>
</music></mei>
